<title>INDIA: India's M3 money supply growth eases to 15.1 pct.</title>
<headline>India's M3 money supply growth eases to 15.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's year-on-year M3 money supply growth eased to 15.1 percent on October 25 from 15.7 percent a fortnight ago, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.  </p>
<p>		   M3 MONEY SUPPLY GROWTH (yr-on-yr in pct)</p>
<p>		   Oct 25, 1996   Oct 11, 1996  Oct 27, 1995</p>
<p>		   15.1		15.7	     14.19</p>
<p>Money supply was 6,465.49 billion rupees on October 25 compared to 6,438.27 billion rupees on October 11, 1996 and 5,593.01 billion on October 27, 1995, the RBI said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
